# Accepted findings, with reasons. Anything not listed here fails CI.
# Review this file when the modules change.

# AWS-0104 Security group rule allows unrestricted egress to any IP address.
# The tasks need HTTPS out to pull images, write logs, read secrets and call
# third party APIs. The rule is limited to port 443; the destination cannot be
# narrowed without knowing every endpoint the application talks to. Set
# enable_vpc_endpoints on the network module to keep AWS service traffic inside
# the VPC, and add narrower rules through additional_egress_rules.
AWS-0104

# AWS-0053 Load balancer is exposed publicly.
# This module builds a public web service, so the load balancer is
# internet facing by default. Reachability is controlled by the security group,
# which requires alb_ingress_cidrs or alb_ingress_prefix_list_ids and has no
# default. Set internal = true when traffic arrives over a private link.
AWS-0053

# AWS-0132 Bucket does not encrypt with a customer managed key.
# The load balancer access log bucket is SSE-S3. See the note in
# alb-access-logs.tf: some log delivery paths do not support a customer managed
# key, and a bucket that silently rejects log writes is worse than one using an
# AWS managed key.
AWS-0132
